2. Encryption Controls
	•	At rest: Encrypt all stored model weights, fine-tuning data, logs, and results. Use CMKs for sensitive workloads.
	•	In transit: Use TLS 1.2+ for all API calls, possibly mTLS (mutual TLS) for high-sensitivity.
	•	Granular control: Decide what is encrypted with platform keys vs your own HSM keys.
	•	Impact: Stops data leakage if storage or communication is compromised.

